# Build context filter for Dockerfile (API) and Dockerfile.web.
#
# Docker matches these patterns from the context root, so a bare `node_modules` only
# excludes the root folder: nested folders need `**/`.
#
# KEEP INCLUDED (the images read them): `files/` (SCAA flavour wheel data),
# `packages/db/drizzle/` (committed migrations + journal), `apps/web/public/` (static
# assets), `apps/api/src/templates/` (email templates) and every workspace manifest.
#
# Exceptions (`!` lines) name exact paths only. A `**/` exception makes Docker walk into
# every excluded folder to look for re-included files, and an unreadable one (the postgres
# data folder `data/postgres` is mode 0700, owned by uid 999) then fails the build with
# "permission denied". A new template in another folder needs its own `!` line.
# scripts/ci/dockerignore.test.sh checks these rules.

# Dependencies and build or test output, at any depth.
**/node_modules
**/coverage
**/dist
**/.turbo

# VCS, CI and editor or agent tooling.
.git
.github
.claude
.kiro
.opencode
.vscode
.idea

# Local data: uploaded photos, the postgres data folder and database backups never belong
# in an image (the self-hosting guide creates data/, backups/, backup-export/ and
# uploads-rescue/ inside the checkout, and writes dumps and archives into it).
uploads
**/uploads
backups
data
backup-export
uploads-rescue
**/*.dump
**/uploads-*.tar.gz

# Documentation and planning (no build step reads them).
plans
openspec
docs

# Local Garage config (holds secrets; garage.toml.example stays).
garage.toml

# Keep local env / secret files out of the published images.
# Both Dockerfile and Dockerfile.web use `COPY . .`, so without these exclusions
# a populated .env would bake a developer's real secrets into the PUBLIC image.
# The three committed *.env.example templates are re-included below by exact path.
.env
*.env
.env.*
**/*.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!apps/api/.env.example
!apps/web/.env.example
